  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse the actual original modular ratios and native removable singularities, rather than introducing a separate meromorphic function sheaf. Reuse the established boundedness dictionary and isolated zero lemmas to avoid duplicate complex/upper-half-plane topology. Native cusp analytic factorization, finite congruence quotient and discriminant decay supply the one exponent needed for all cusps. Reuse the existing modular restriction and actual norm integrality consumer. All preceding representation assumptions are discharged in the explicit original field consumer; the next finite-place exhaustion uses already proved Dedekind-center localization and integral-closure containment.",
